From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom: initialize shared TZ tables for MSM8226

The exact Samsung MSM8226 BSP runs msm_iommu_sec_ptbl_init() from its
secure-driver subsys_initcall when any enabled IOMMU has a secure ID.
This precedes the non-secure display-context attach and is independent
of which contexts clients actually use.

The current diagnostic DT describes only the non-secure MDP context.
qcom_iommu therefore skips this shared TZ setup when it checks for
secure context children. Match the BSP initialization requirement using
the existing once-only secure-table helper, restricted to MSM8226 match
data. Keep firmware-service errors fatal and preserve the existing
retained-allocation handling. No protected global-register access or
new firmware ABI is added.

Hardware ATOS repeatedly ignored the Linux test section mapping and
its removal, returning the same unrelated physical address. This is
a further evidenced missing BSP step; physical scanout and translation
validation are still required.

Link: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226/blob/3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256/drivers/iommu/msm_iommu-sec.c

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 37a319bef..d037585cc 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@ struct qcom_iommu_cfg {
 	/* Faulting transactions must terminate rather than stall. */
 	bool no_stall;
 	bool halt;
+	/* Older TZ initializes shared tables even for non-secure clients. */
+	bool needs_secure_ptbl;
 	u32 actlr;
 	const struct qcom_iommu_bfb_reg *bfb;
 	unsigned int num_bfb;
@@ -983,7 +985,8 @@ static int qcom_iommu_device_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
-	if (qcom_iommu_has_secure_context(qcom_iommu)) {
+	if (qcom_iommu_has_secure_context(qcom_iommu) ||
+	    (qcom_iommu->cfg && qcom_iommu->cfg->needs_secure_ptbl)) {
 		ret = qcom_iommu_sec_ptbl_init(dev);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dev, "cannot init secure pg table(%d)\n", ret);
@@ -1113,6 +1116,7 @@ static const struct qcom_iommu_bfb_reg msm8226_mdp_bfb[] = {
 static const struct qcom_iommu_cfg msm8226_mdp_cfg = {
 	.no_stall = true,
 	.halt = true,
+	.needs_secure_ptbl = true,
 	/* BPRCOSH/ISH/NSH: direct cacheable requests to the L2 slave port. */
 	.actlr = GENMASK(30, 28),
 	.bfb = msm8226_mdp_bfb,
